course: dictionary
lesson: 10672
title: Clues in context: unmotivated
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The start of a word can be a clue. Un- often means "not", so unmotivated means not motivated: not wanting to try, and without the energy or interest to do something. Motivate means to give someone a reason to act, so an unmotivated person has no spark to get going.
explain: Read the words around the word. «"Needs encouragement" on a report usually means the pupil is lazy or unmotivated (does not want to try).» Encouragement means help to feel keen, so a pupil who needs it is one who is not keen yet. The clue words point you to the meaning.
explain: Formal writing uses the word in another way. An unmotivated action has no clear reason behind it, so it is about the action, not about a person's feelings. To check your meaning, swap it into the sentence: "The pupil was unmotivated" should still make sense when you read it as "did not want to try".
fact: Unmotivated means not wanting to do something, without the energy or interest to try.
fact: The word «unmotivated» can also be formal: an unmotivated action has no clear reason behind it.
fact: The prefix un- often means "not", so «unmotivated» is the opposite of motivated.
fact: Teachers and coaches try to motivate pupils who feel unmotivated.
fact: In plain speech, UK people might say "can't be bothered" instead.
exercise: «"Needs encouragement" on a report usually means the pupil is lazy or unmotivated.» What does unmotivated mean? | *Not wanting to try, with no energy or interest | Very quick at running and always first | Full of energy and keen to start every task | Happy to be given extra homework
exercise: In the same sentence, which word is the clue that helps you work out the meaning? | pupil | usually | *encouragement | report
exercise: In a news story, an «unmotivated» crime means what? | *A crime with no clear reason behind it | A crime that was filmed on a phone | A crime solved by the police in one day | A crime planned for a whole year
test: Which word is the opposite of unmotivated? | *Motivated | Late | Sleepy | Bored
test: Jayden says he feels unmotivated about tidying his room. What does he mean? | He is too busy to speak | *He does not want to try, and has no energy for it | He has lost his room | He is very tidy and loves cleaning
exam: Which sentence uses «unmotivated» in the formal way? | Ella felt unmotivated, so she stayed in bed all morning | Tom did his homework with great keenness every night | The coach tried hard to motivate the team before the match | *The police said the attack was unmotivated, with no clear reason
